  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1250 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nStarting Tuesday through Thursday, latest global model guidance \ndoes bring dry weather conditions back to the region. Zonal H500 \nsynoptic pattern with the main steering flow across the northern \nCONUS and the Gulf keeps any disturbances confined to these \nregions. Going towards the end of the week, the southern stream \njet becomes more active with a potential disturbance with its \norigins near Baja California gets absorbed in mid level trough \npattern to bing rain chances back to the southern High Plains \ntowards the end of the forecast period. High temperatures mid \nweek will moderate to slightly above average before returning to \nnear average as we approach the end of the month of October.",
